# BigBlueButton 3.x Development Rules

You are working on a customized fork of BigBlueButton (BBB) version 3.x.

This project is NOT a generic React application.
It is a large-scale realtime conferencing platform with tightly coupled frontend/backend architecture based on WebRTC, GraphQL, realtime synchronization, mediasoup/SFU, Redis, and BBB backend services.

You MUST follow these rules strictly.

---

# PROJECT CONTEXT

This repository is a fork of:

https://github.com/bigbluebutton/bigbluebutton

Target branch:

v3.0.x-release

The project goal is:

* Customize and redesign the BBB frontend
* Extend meeting UI/UX
* Add custom realtime features
* Keep compatibility with upstream BBB updates
* Avoid breaking core BBB architecture
* Maintain upgradeability

Development environment:

* Frontend runs locally on macOS
* Backend/realtime services run on a production/staging BBB Ubuntu server

Architecture:

MacBook React Dev Environment
↓
Production BBB Server
↓
Realtime APIs/WebSocket/WebRTC

